reply-to: andy.vesper@eng.pko.dec.com
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


"Jason,Choi" <jhchoi@otech.otech.co.kr> writes:

>I tried to find out how to get color text at DECterm in OpenVMS/AXP
>for days. but just failed.

>But I couldn't find out how to get RED "hello, world" or BLUE "hello,
>world" at DECterm in OpenVMS/AXP.

$ esc[0,8] = 27
$ write sys$output esc, "[41mHello, World!", esc, "[m"

Works for me!

You do have a color display, I hope :-)

For your reference:

	30	black
	31	red
	32	green
	33	yellow
	34	blue
	35	magenta
	36	cyan
	37	white
	38	white
	39	white

(I think some of the `white' entries here are really `default', so they
might not be white if you have different default colors.)

Change the first digit to `4' (i.e. 41, 42...) and you set the color
for the background of the letters.

Andy V



