n.kraaijeveld@sepa.tudelft.nl (Niels Kraaijeveld) wrote:
>Hi SCSI expert,
>
>I have documentation about my SCSI HD (Digital DSP3000L Series), but
>for a non-SCSI expert it is very brief. So can anyone tell my anything
>about (or where can I find good detailled documentation):
>
>- notification of AC power failure
Spits out any cached write data and retracts the actuator. Stops responding
to commands. Active low input.

>- spindle synchronization
Synchronize multiple spindles in a system by connecting this pin across all
of them. Bidirectional TTL open collector.

>- write protection
Now that's easy isn't it? Active low input.

>- spin delay
Do not spin up at power up (wait for a START UNIT or wait a certain time defined
in the mode pages.) Active low input.

It's all in the manual or installation guide.

>
>And what is the best  configuration for the HD.
Just make sure write caching is on. Set the WCE bit in the caching mode page.
Get yourself DSP tools to do that. E.g. at 
http://www.vobis.de/bbs/firmen/quantum/tools/index.html

Hope this helps,
Ralf-Peter
