In article <4ek2d3$ca0_001@news.fast.net>, kshuff@fast.net (kshuff) writes:

>Need to make a standalone backup and boot tapes for Ultrix 3.1. Any help or 
>suggestions appreciated.

The backup is easy if you have a tape drive.  Shutdown to single
user and backup the file systems with dump.  If they can fit on
a single tape, use the norewind device between file systems.

The boot tape may also be easy, if you have the installation tapes;
just make a copy of the boot tape.  The standalone system has the tools
needed to make a file system and restore a dump format backup.
Once you restore the root, you can boot that to single user and
use it to restore anything else.  The CDROM also has the standalone
system.

A standalone backup that restores itself is hard, since it requires
rewriting the on-tape standalone file system.  I think the tools for
that were only included in the source distribution.


