I also have an AXP 150. Here is a summary of my experience 
with the memory:

There are two banks of memory. Each Bank if composed of 4 memory 
slots. All odd slots are bank 0. All even slots are bank 1. 
(consider slot 1 as being next to the power supply). You cannot 
partially fill a bank. This means you will either have 4 memory 
boards or 8 installed. Also all memory within a bank must be 
identical. The memory density must be either 4mb/board or 
16mb/board. My documentation is a little fuzzy on this, but I have 
run the following combinations successfully: 4 4mb boards (16mb 
total), 8 4mb boards(32mb tot), 4 16mb boards(64mb tot), 4 16 and 
4 4mb boards (80 mb tot).  Also I am running mixed speeds-The 16mb 
boards are 60ns while the 4mb boards are 70ns. Hope this helps.



