daniel@synchrods.synchrods.com (Daniel Senderowicz) wrote:
>Folks,
>
>
>However I'm now having a different problem: The TK50 is stuck,
>the red light keeps blinking, so I push it in and out a few
>times, then it settles, it seems to make the tape move for a
>couple of seconds and after a while goes back into the blinking
>mood. The main problem is that as it is now I can't remove the
>tape in which I have the system. Is there any way to reset this,
>and/or taking the tape out without resorting to placing the
>device under the wheels of my diesel truck? Thanks in advance,

There are two possibilities: Either the tape's leader has been loaded 
into the drive, or all of the tape is still in the cartridge.

If the former is true, you may have problems if you want to recover the 
tape.

If all of the tape is still in the cartridge, it's pretty easy.  Remove 
the TK50 from the machine.  If you can't see the takeup reel, you may 
need to remove the sheet metal cover at the back of the drive.  I think 
that three screws hold it on.  If the tape has not been pulled into the 
drive, find the solenoid at the front of the drive, near the red 
button.  It engages a white piece of plastic which locks the cartridge 
in place. Release this and the cartridge should pop out.

There is a plastic leader attached to the takeup drum which is used to 
"snag" the tape out of the cartridge. Sometimes this leader breaks or 
comes off the plastic hook used to hold it in place. If this is the 
case, replacing the leader may fix the drive.

Good luck!

