senderow@diva.EECS.Berkeley.EDU (Dan Senderowicz) wrote:
>Here is the problem: I have a VAXStation II/GPX with a TK50
>drive, a Dilog SCSI controller and a RZ55 with nothing on it
>(yet). When I turn it on, it prompts me with the language
>selection and after accepting my entry it goes through the
>normal tests down to 3, which it passes OK. When it gets to the
>"loading system software" it goes into "?54 RETRY". I tried to
>stop it and go to the console prompt (>>>) using ^C and any
>other imaginable combination of keys without success. I also
>tried to stop it at earlier stages of the test but again nothing
>happens. This problem also happened with another configuration
>that I had earlier (before the disk died), that is a MFM disk
>and corresponding controller RQDX3. Is this a CPU board problem
>or what? I'll appreciate any help. Regards,
>

The MicroVax II and its workstation variants have a "HALT ENABLE" switch
on the back near the console connector.  This is a 2 position toggle 
switch that I believe was labled with a circle and a dot in the center.
With halts enabled the system will stop the power up self test at 3 and 
drop to the >>> prompt.  

There should be a halt button on the front of the system that you can 
use to halt it, assuming the halts are enabled.

One side effect of enabling halts is that it disables the autoboot and 
autorestart functions.

In normal operation, you shouldn't see the language prompt on power up.
There is a 3 position rotary switch on the back that is probably in the 
"talking head" position.  This switch should be in the middle position.

