>your syntax above is wrong:  You don't want:
>	$cdc ==: www http://www.cdc.gov
>rather, you'd want:
>	$cdc :== www http://www.cdc.gov
>Of course, that won't actually run any program, but at least it'll give you a
>definition of the symbol CDC instead of the error message:
>	%DCL-W-EXPSYN, invalid expression syntax - check operators and operands

The above assumes that www is defined as a DCL command (i.e., in DCLTABLES).
First type:

  $ show symbol www

If you see something like: "%DCL-W-UNDSYM, undefined symbol", then what
Carl has recommended should work.

However, if you see something like: WWW == "$ xxx:[xxx]xxx", then you'll have
to define CDC as:

  $ cdc == www + " http://www.cdc.gov"

