Bradford A Lubell (lubell@eisner.decus.org) wrote:
: Does anybody have any experience with connecting an HP LaserJet 4MV to a
: OpenVMS system via either UCX (TCP/IP) or LAT?

Sure.

I have installed a HP 4M+ on our network. It boots from a DEC 2000 machine
using BOOTP. This works OK execept it will not start TFTP to get the printer
configuration file. This implies that you can only set the ip address, not 
configure the interface (e.g. limit the access).
Then I have created lpr queues (using the ucx$lprsetup program) to 
access the printer (you need two queues, one for text files and one for any 
other files).

Thus it works, but if you have problems with unauthorized use etc., you
must find another machine to boot from.

The configuration is VMS/alpha 6.1 with UCX 3.1.

