bbassore@ix.netcom.com(Brad D. Bassore ) wrote:
>Does somebody out there know what the standard configuration and
>specifications of a DEC Workstation 2000 is. I was recently give one by
>a friend. It has a VS410 AA Processor unit along with a RD54 RA Hard
>Drive and a TK 50ZFA Tape Drive. I am curious what type of processor
>this machine has along with the amount of ram (I assume it has't been
>upgraded). Also how many megabytes is the hard drive and tape? Thanks
>in advance. Brad D. Bassore
>bbassore@ix.netcom.com

The VS410-AA has a MicroVAX II CPU.  It also contains 2MB of memory and 
a monochrome 1024x864 video controller on the board.  Normally, there is 
also a daughterboard with and additional 2MB or 4MB of memory, although 
I believe there is also a 12MB daughterboard available (I've never seen 
one.)  Optionally, there may also be a daughterboard which is a color 
1024x864 video controller.

In summary, depending on configuration, the VS2000 may be 2MB, 4MB, 6MB, 
or 14MB, with monochrome graphics, and may or may not have color 
graphics.

The console command "TEST 50" will report the exact configuration, but 
you have to know how to read the output.

The RD54 disk is a Maxtor 2190 disk.  It formats out to about 159MB.

The TK50Z-FA tape drive is a 95MB tape drive.

