From: you@somehost.somedomain (Garrick)
Subject: Re: Unix to VMS printing?
Date: 1996/01/21
Message-ID: <4dtf67$g46@news.ust.hk>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 136003789
references: <4ccahm$83s@news.jhu.edu>
organization: Win95
content-type: Text/Plain; charset=ISO-8859-1
mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

In article <4ccahm$83s@news.jhu.edu>, gerdes says...
>
>We have a PostScript printer that's mounted on a VAX 4000/60, and
>would like to use it to print from a DEC 3000/700 running Digital Unix.
>How should we setup /etc/printcap and the print queue on the local (VMS)
>machine to make this work?

First, UCX should be installed on your VAX station and the LPD service should 
be enabled.

Then using the lprsetup utility in the VAX to set up a TCP server queue.  
During the configuration, you should specify the printer server queue name in 
the VAX station.

In the Unix side, the printcap file should be as followed,

	choose remote printing	
	parameter rm = remote node = VAX machine node name
	printer should be the name of the printer server queue in VAX


Garrick

	
	




