: Hi,

: I'm trying to set up a DEC 5000/200 with a 1 Gig RZ57 drive.  The
: Ultrix install went fine, I put the root partition on a smaller 300
: meg disk.  But I'm having problems using the 1 gig drive.  When I
: chpt the drive I see this:

: # chpt -q /dev/rrz0c
: /dev/rrz0c
: Current partition table:
: partition     bottom        top       size    overlap
:     a              0      32767      32768    c
:     b          32768     217087     184320    c
:     c              0    1954049    1954050    a,b,d,e,f,g,h
:     d         831488    1130495     299008    c,h
:     e        1130496    1429503     299008    c,h
:     f        1429504    1954049     524546    c,h
:     g         217088     831487     614400    c
:     h         831488    1954049    1122562    c,d,e,f

: I then tried mounting /dev/rz0c as /home.  That works too, but the
: c partition doesn't seem to contain everything.   So when I do a 'df'
: it shows

: # df
: Filesystem                   Total    kbytes   kbytes   %     
: node                         kbytes   used     free     used  Mounted on
: /dev/rz0c                     15823      9     14232    0%   /home
: ...

: From the partition table I assume that 'c' spawns the whole disk.  So
: I should get the whole 1 gig.  But why isn't that the case here?

: I'm fairly new at sysadmin, so please don't flame me.  :-)  Thanks in
: advance for any advice you can give me.

Sounds like you newfs'd /dev/rrz0a.  Because both rz0a and rz0c start
at block 0, you can (sort of) use them interchangably.  Try newfs'ing
/dev/rrz0c and see if you have any better luck.  The first few lines
of newfs should look something like:

Warning: 227 sector(s) in last cylinder unallocated
/dev/rrz2c:     1954048 sectors in 1835 cylinders of 15 tracks, 71 sectors
        1000.5Mb in 115 cyl groups (16 c/g, 8.72Mb/g, 2048 i/g)
super-block backups (for fsck -b#) at:
 32, 17152, 34272, 51392, 68512, 85632, 102752, 119872, 136992, 154112,

Note the 3rd line that says 1000.5Mb.

Simon.
