In article <4dmnk2$po3@bigboote.WPI.EDU>, joev@pyramid.res.wpi.edu (Joseph Vigneau) writes:

:Does anyone have any experience in dual booting a DEC 2000/300 Jensen with
:NT Workstation and Digital Unix?

  Yes, there are folks around that have this configuration. 

  You will need at least one disk for each operating system in use, and
  you will need the appropriate Digital and Microsoft software licenses.

  You will end up becoming familiar with the PALcode-level operations, as
  Microsoft NT requires the (Microsoft-specified) ARC console, while both
  OpenVMS and UNIX require the (Digital-specified) SRM console...  Moving
  between ARC and SRM involves some (documented) console-level commands.

  Current PALcode for all Alpha systems is available on CD-ROM, and also
  at Digital's web site.

