>Hi,
>
>I have a customer with 120 PC's running DEC's DECnet Pathworks 
>on Windows95 that need to access some NFS servers. DEC doesn't have 
>an NFS solution for PC's so I'm trying to get PC-NFSPro 2.0 or 
>FTP's Interdrive-95 to work but without much success. (FTP's 
>Interdrive95 does claim to be compatible with Pathworks but I haven't 
>yet spoken to anyone at FTP software who is familiar with it).

   You don't say exactly what you're having problems with.
   Both of these solutions should work:
   Under Win95, you can bind both the FTP and MS client to the MS IP stack 
(this happens by default) - the MS client should allow you to access 
Pathworks servers over IP and the FTP client will let you at the NFS mounts.
   Under Pro, if you "Enable NetBIOS Services", you can bind both the MS 
client and the Sunsoft client to the Sunsoft IP stack (also the default).
   If you don't need DECNET-specific features, you could then consider going 
to an IP-only solution.
   Not the answer you were looking for, but it might help.

