In article <1996Jan23.094459@axp2.umkc.edu>, mcdonald@axp2.umkc.edu (Gary Lee McDonald) writes:
> 
> Greetings,
> 
>   In the following output from $ show mem, 
> what are the zero free pages in the
> Granularity Hint Regions section telling me?  
> Is there a section I can read in 
> the docs about this?  Many thanks for any enlightenment!
> 
<snip: SHOW MEM output>

 See The Book of Ruth (a.k.a. "OpenVMS AXP Internals and Data Structures":)
 and look in the index under "Granularity Hint Regions" and "Huge pages"

 briefly, hugh pages are collections of virtually contiguous pages of
 memory that are also physically contiguous, enableing AXP translation
 buffer performance gains. The executive routinely makes use of this
 feature for code and data that are permanently mapped. Am implication
 of these restraints is that pages in such a region cannot be free.

 Hope this helps.
