The boards from the pair of MicroVAX IIs - now I've worked out what
they all are. Thought you all might like to see what the mystery
boards I asked about were.

exhibit 1, MicroVAX II 

Contains: 

- Processor
- M7607 (1Mb RAM)
- M7504 (DEQNA ethernet?)
- Emulex 16 port serial board 
- M7546 (TK50 controller?)
- Emulex MSCP disk controller
- A pair of non-DEC boards -  turns out to be an interface for a 
                              Transputer module
  
exhibit 2, MicroVAX II

Contains:

- Processor
- Non-DEC (EMC ?) RAM board - unknown size - Quad height, fully populated
- Another Non-DEC (EMC ?) RAM board - unknown size - Quad height, fully populated
- M9047 - QBus grant cty
- M3106 (four serial ports)
- Emulex disk controller
- M7546 (TK50 controller)
- RQRX controller (for RX50 and RD53)
- M9047 (Qbus grant cty)
- M9047 (Qbus grant cty)

>This latter MicroVAX has an internal RD53 (Micropolis) drive
>fitted. The drive is very noisy (squealing sounds) but may be hushed
>up by wedging a screwdriver under one of the rear rubber mounts, so
>there is hope for it!

This RD53 drive turned out to be caput - not responding to the controller.

>There are three similar sized expansion cabinets, containing one heavy
>Fujitsu M2333K (8038-4765-8003A) drive each, together with power
>supply.

These all work though!

Thanks for all the advice concerning TK50s ...

