Anyhow, I've reconfigured the machines. Machine 1, I shall keep, so I
want the best spec I can have ;) Machine 2 will take what is left.

Machine 1:

1 - Processor (according to the docs, with 1Mb on board)
2 - Third party (EMC) RAM board
3 - Third party (EMC) RAM board
4 - DZQ11 4 port serial (M3106)
5 - DEQNA (M7504)
6 - TK50 controller (M7546)
7 - Emulex MSCP controller
also  -  Grant cty cards where required ...

This machine has an internal TK50 and will interface to one external
Fujitsu drive.

Machine 2:

1 - Processor (according to the docs, with 1Mb on board)
2 - 1Mb RAM (M7607)
3 - Emulex MSCP controller
   No grant cty cards required

This system has no TK50, and will interface to one or two external
Fujitsu drives.

Spare boards:

1 x EMC RAM board (unknown size - quad height)
1 x Emulex 16 port serial board, with distribution panel
1 x RXRQ controller (I have no devices for this to talk to ;)
1 x TK50 controller (ditto)
1 x Pair of boards to interface to Transputer module (no module)
3 x Grant cty cards

errm, that's it.

I have got machine 1 to boot from one of the Fujitsu drives. After
some messing about VMS (5.4) came up, and I was able to log in as
SYSTEM. I know little about VMS, but "SHOW MEMORY" reported 16Mb. Can
