In article <4e3umm$sp7@info-server.bbn.com>, bkort@labs-n.bbn.com () writes:
> Can a KLESI-SA (TU81E Tape Controller) be used with a TU80 tape drive?

  No. The TU80 has a formatted Pertec interface. The TU81 family has an extra
logic board in the drive that converts it to the LESI interface.

> Are all TKQ50 Controllers able to read/write TK70 tape drives, or
> is there some minimum revision level before it will write on a TK70?

  The TQK50 can write to a truly blank TK70 tape (no cal tracks on the tape).
I am told there's a revision dependency, but I don't know what it is. If your
TQK50 has the 065 gate array (it's a 24- or 28-pin package on the controller)
you should be Ok.

  Note that you will get a TK50-format tape out of this which may not read
on other TK50 drives.

