In article <4dk14l$esr@st-james.comp.vuw.ac.nz>, srlnrow@alpha.gns.cri.nz writes:

>In DECwindows Motif, how can it happen that the Workspace menu is no longer
>available for a particular user, but is for others?
>...
>The user doesn't get a
>menu when clicking on the background root window, and the the Workspace menu
>choice in the Window menu (the top left button off a window) is greyed out and
>not able to be selected.

And the answer is:

because of the existance of a file named .;1 in SYS$LOGIN. (That is, a
file named simply ".") Apparently, this file matches whatever code is used to
open DECW$MWM_RC.DAT and so the correct configuration is never found.

