In article <4e5hta$q3i@Trademart-1.EDnet.NS.CA>, 
arthur_dave@burridge.nscc.ns.ca (Dave Arthur) writes:

Re: DEC M8739 board

> The board is a quad UNIBUS card, It has a 50 pin berg connector on one
> side.
> Silk Screen 5014691D1-P1 M8739
> On the solder side AZTEC UNIBUS Adapter card

It is a Unibus interface to the RC25 dual-platter disk drive,
one of the strangest ideas that DEC ever had for a disk drive.

It had two platters, one fixed and one removable.   The idea
was that you would have your system disk on the fixed platter,
with the removable disk for user data, backups, etc.   The
problem was that there was only a single motor.   If you
spun down the removable cartridge, your system disk was spun
down also!

Many of us think that the RC25 must have somehow escaped from
the UPG.

