chungto@ampex.com (Tony Chung) writes:

>Normally, on SunOS, you use vmstat to monitor
>swap usage.
>
>What about on alpha-dec-osf?
>
>man -k swap or the sys adm book has no
>information at all.

If "man -k swap" fails to find swapon(8) your man pages are not properly
installed.

    ues5:~ 3> swapon -s
    Swap partition /dev/rz1b:
	Allocated space:        16384 pages (128MB)
	In-use space:             109 pages (  0%)
	Free space:             16275 pages ( 99%)


    Total swap allocation:
	Allocated space:        16384 pages (128MB)
	In-use space:             109 pages (  0%)
	Available space:        16275 pages ( 99%)

In addition to vmstat (which is available) there is a Motif application
called vmubc (ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/Digital/vmubc.tar.Z), but you 
have to download and compile it yourself.  

Dan
