The fastest alpha machines from DEC are the 300Mhz EV5 machines. The 
Alphastation 6/300 or the Alphaserver 8200 or 8400. The Alphastation is a 
single CPU the Alphaservers are large servers which can be multi CPU and
large memory machines. Aspen or Carrera have both 300Mhz and 333Mhz boxes I
belive. I expect DEC to have 333Mhz boxes out shortly. 

You didn't mention what operating system you were going to use. The DEC ones
will run OSF and VMS, possibly NT on the Alphastation. Either Aspen or 
Carrera can offer OSF, VMS, NT and Linux I believe.

That represents the current situation, I guess machines with the EV56 400Mhz 
chip will be available sometime in the not too distant future as well. 


