In article <N.Goldman-1801961045200001@ng-mac1.gen.cam.ac.uk>,
N.Goldman@gen.cam.ac.uk (Nick Goldman) writes:
>Is there any way I can use my DEC DAT drive (TLZ07) to back-up my Toshiba
>laptop PC (running MS-DOS 6.22 and Windows 3.11)?
>
>It hurts to have to buy a different tape backup device for the laptop,
>after spending so much on the one for my workstation.
>
>If it CAN be done, please send full instructions.


There is a product called 'StorageWorks Desktop Backup' (previous name
was 'PathWorks Desktop Backup'). It is a server software that needs to
be installed on your system and includes clients for MS-DOS, MS-Windows,
Mac (and newer versions also MS-Windows-NT I think). The version I have
supports DECnet and AppleTalk as the transport (and newer versions also
TCP/IP I think).

I run the server software on OpenVMS and use it with MS-Windows clients.
It runs quite fast.

