Eddy Austin <edward@liv.ac.uk> wrote:
>this may seem a silly question (thereagain most of my friends think i'm silly
>having a 3100/38 instead of a PC!!) but how do I open up this machine, I want
>to add another scsi drive.
>
>I have looked but only manage to open the front compartment :-(

If you look at the back of the machine, there are two captive screws, 
one on each side. You need to loosen these until they are dangling.  
They shouldn't come out.

Then, the cover will slide off to the front.  On most machines the 
cover is pretty tight and I usually need to give it a sharp "pop" to 
get it off.  Just remember that the cover slide straight out to the 
front.  It doesn't lift up.

