>
>this may seem a silly question (thereagain most of my friends think i'm silly
>having a 3100/38 instead of a PC!!) but how do I open up this machine, I want
>to add another scsi drive.
>
>I have looked but only manage to open the front compartment :-(

On the back of the computer there are two philips screws
on the left and right sides (they are in moderately deep holes).
Unscrew these two, and you will then be able to slide the cover
off (sliding towards the back).

I'm not sure of the 3100/38, but you may need special mounting
hardware to attach a new drive, but there is usually a spare
scsi connecter and power connector laying around inside.

It's usually quite easy to add a new drive once you've gotten
the correct mounting hardware.



