Robin Birch (robin@falstaf.demon.co.uk) wrote:
: Dear All,
: Just a chaser on something I posted earlier:

: Does any body have the switch settings for a viking scsi controller
: for an exabyte.  Failing this has somebody got the address/fax number
: for viking.

: The controller is a VIK/QTO

This controller was made by TD systems.  It is Q-bus, mag tape only,
TMSCP support.  (It was also made in disk only, MSCP, and both at the
same time).  It has no switches.  It does have 4 jumpers, which allows
you to select the memory address the device registers show up at.
The controller is configured for devices by connecting an RS-232 terminal
to some unused pins on the SCSI port.  They supply a little junction
board with 2 50-pin headers and a 25-pin RS-232 connector on it.  Do you
have this part?  If so, just insert it in the scsi cable and plug in a
terminal.  Hit return a couple of times, and the monitor on the card will
give you a menu.  (Set the terminal to 9600 baud, 8 bit, no parity.)
If you need more details, or if you can't find the junction board, let
me know.  I have a full set of TD documentation somewhere around here.
The controller does a GREAT job of working around the many quirks of the
Exabyte drive and making it totally compatible with TMSCP.



