:Eric Smith (eric@goonsquad.spies.com) wrote:
:
:: I just bought a VAXstation 3520.  I'm not sure if I got a good deal or
:: not, but I didn't pay too much.
:
:: Can anyone tell me the general specs?  Which generation of VAX CPU
:: does it use?  Are there newer plug-compatible VAX CPU cards I could
:: put in to upgrade it?
:
:: I didn't get a monitor with it; which DEC monitors are compatible?
:
:That's a dual CPU version of the 3500, which uses the KA650 CPU,
:same as the VAXserver 3600 and MicroVAX III.
:
:You can bring it up with a VT100 console plugged into the MMJ
:connector on the CPU if you don't have monitor.

  The VAXstation 3520 -- the "Firefox" -- is a dual-processor CVAX
  workstation system, with each processor on the dual-processor CPU
  modules used in the system having roughly the same performance as
  the VAXstation 3500 processor module.  

  The Firefox internal interconnect (the M-bus) bus design, the Firefox
  memory subsystem (MS60 memory), graphics (VCB03), etc., are all quite
  different from the components of KA650 series processors.  The system
  can be upgraded to a quad SMP processor.  A Q-bus is optional on this
  system and supports specific Q-bus modules, and it requires the
  installation of an M-bus-to-Q-bus adapter (DWFQA) module.

  The original monitor was the VR295, a 1280 x 1024 x 66 Hz monitor.
  Any monitor that supports this combination should be compatible.

