Get yourself a PostScript manual.  From _PostScript Language Reference Manual_
from Adobe Systems, Inc.,
	limitcheck (error)
		A PostScript implementation limit has been exceeded (e.g., too
		many files have been opened simultaneously, or a path has
		become too complex).  Appendix B gives the actual values for
		all such limits [for an Apple LaserWriter].
Since you're not talking about an Apple LaserWriter here, I'll skip the values
for it and simply list the things which had limits for it:
    integer		maximum and mininum values of an integer
    real		simililarly for floating point numbers
    array		maximum array length
    dictionary		maximum number of key/value pairs in a dictionary
    string		maximum string length
    name		maximum number of characters in a name
    file		maximum number of open files
    userdict		capacity of userdict
    operand stack	maximum depth of the operand stack
    dict stack		maximum depth of the dictionary stack
    exec stack		maximum depth of the execution stack
    interpreter level	maximun number of recursive invocations of the
			PostScript interpreter
    save level		maximum number of active saves
    gsave level		maximum number of active gsaves
    path		maximum number of points specified in _all_ active
			path descriptions, including the current path, clip
			path, and paths saved by save and gsave
    dash		maximum number of elements in a dash pattern
    VM			maximum size of virtual memory in bytes
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
