Seung-Jo Baek. (sjbaek@vivace.postech.ac.kr) wrote:
: Hi. DEC users..
: I'm curious how to setup a new SCSI device on AlphaStation200-4/233
: running DigitalUnix V3.3C...
: I've tried to connect 233MB removable Bernoulli disk(IOMEGA) to
: this system...
: I've set SCSI #, external termination etc..
: But, when I mount it to /mnt(as followings), "no such device...."
: messages
: %mount /dev/rrz5a /mnt
:     (SCSI number of IOMEGA disk was 5)
: Any ideas?
: Thans in advance...
: Have a nice day~

First off, you don't want to use the raw device for mount (ever), it
doesn't use that.  You wan to use the cooked device (/dev/rz5a).

Second, you need to make sure that the device has been in the kernel
(look in /sys/conf for your kernel).

Third, make sure that you've made the appropriate device with MAKEDEV
(DEC UNIX follows the BSD loosy-goosiness between dev names and scsi'id's
so you need to check the minor device numbers).  Good info can be had
by saying "man rz"

-Ron




