>
>>And it won't run Digital UNIX or OpenVMS.  Even if you are willing to
>>pay for them..                   ^^^^^^^
>
>THAT ANSWERS MY QUESTION!!!!!!  Ain't that a shame!


The XL was specifically designed NOT to run Unix or OpenVMS.  In that 
way, Digital was able to keep its costs down (fewer components, but more 
important, less testing and certification required), and to keep the 
street price of an Alpha/NT system down.  It also was designed as a 
machine that would be sold strictly through the channel -- not by 
Digital's own sales force.  For OpenVMS or Unix, you have to look at a 
different approach.

Stephen Lawton




