We have a number of DECagent90's scattered around our network,
managed with DEC HUBwatch. We have something of a reliability
problem with a number of these, in that for no apparent reason,
the agent will just hang up and disappear from the network.
In this state, they're completely unreachable, even from the
console port, and have to be revived by power off and on.

This occurs both with very early versions of the agent, and
with units bought quite recently, and regardless of whether the
agent or a DECbridge90 is the hub manager.

In some areas, there's also a noticeable difference in response times 
between agents installed at different points on the same riser cable,
even when the loading on the respective hubs is light and about the same
level.

Has anybody else noticed this problem? Is there a workaround?
Am I doing something wrong?

