>>>>> "andyv" == andyv  <andyv@horizons.com> writes:
In article <4cuusa$8uo@news2.noc.netcom.net> andyv@horizons.com writes:

andyv> We have 4 DEC Alphas and only one has any /dev/rmt* files. I
andyv> can not seem to make any of the devices on any of the other
andyv> systems, it comes back with no device present or just no
andyv> device. Should the tape drive be on ID4 or do I have to
andyv> reconfigure the Kernal ? if so how. Any help would be great.

Tape devices are TZ#, though the access point is /dev/rmt# and it
doesn't map one to one.

Say you have a tape device at SCSI id 4, then you would cd to /dev and
do

	./MAKEDEV tz4

and it would make all the /dev/rmt0* files for you.

If you add another tape drive to this system, and it's SCSI id is 3,
then when you do the MAKEDEV, you'll get /dev/rmt1* tape devices.

It's done this way for historical reasons.

