I can't reply directly because your email is configured.

I would choose the 4/233 system, primarily because of the PCI bus. You
can get a wider range of peripherials for that bus, including e.g.,
100-mb/s ethernet. I doubt that DEC will make a 100Base-T interface
for the turbochannel machines.

My guess is also that your memory upgrades would be cheaper on the
400, and you can get better & cheaper graphics options. Also, should
you choose to, you can boot the 400 under Windows/NT or Linux, which
you can't do with the 3000 series.



