> have a 3000/300LX and an AlphaStation 200 4/100.

I have gotten a Pioneer DRM602x to work on a 3000/300LX,
and a VAXstation 4000-90 both under OpenVMS.

I did it without any supplemental executables, which means
it does not gracefully arbitrate conflicting platter
accesses.  The software to do that is more expensive than the
jukebox unit.

If a lot of contention occurs, the unit tends to hang.

You need to do some minor magic to create the device entries
for each of the platters.

Digital doesn't have the SCSI device table entries for the
DRM602x in the 3000/300LX controlware, so it cannot be
used a bootable CDROM.

I'll see if my management will permit me to release the
DCL procedure for declaring the device entries...





