I seem to recall that the 8GB are only possible with compression.

the amount of compression possible varies very much with the type
of data.

If I read you correctly, you say that some diskspace of 6.5GB on
disk(s) A does NOT fit on the tape, while 6.5GB on disk(s) B 
does fit on the tape?

If this is the case, I'd just assume that the possible compression
of the data on disk(s) A is much lower. 

If you come up with a scheme where you must rely on a specific
tape capacity, the only way to go is to switch off any compression.
(Using compression can even result in an increase in total space:
For example if you deal this way already precompressed files 
[ZIP or others] )

uwe



