"Brian A. Duncan" <bad@efogm.msd.ray.com> wrote:
>I need to set up a print queue on an OpenVMS VAX 6.1 system to print to a
>networked QMS 1725 printer. I was told there were some bugs in the driver or
>something of that nature and that it couldn't be done.

Which network card do you have for this printer?  They have gone through
several different versions, including some that spoke only DECNET, some
only TCP/IP, some that spoke both, and their newest (CROWN) which is 
supposed to speak TCP/IP and NetWare.  I've used the old DECNET only and
DECNET-TCP/IP boards with varying degrees of difficulty.  I also have
some experience with the CROWN boards, though not as much.

With the DECNET aware boards they have (or had) special symbionts which
ran the queues.  We run that on VMS 5.4 with only occasional problems now.
The TCP/IP boards do not reliably run the lpd protocol, even the CROWN
boards which claim to.  We use the Multinet Stream Symbiont pointing to
port 35 on the printer to print to printers which have TCP/IP and CROWN
boards.   It works, though like the recent thread on the Dec DCPS printer,
cancelling a job requires some intervention on both the printer and the 
symbiont side.

>Thanks in advance for any help...
You're welcome.  I hope this helps.

Ari
