I have the layered subset for both DS100 and DS200.  You will need an
Ultrix host -- VAX or RISC -- with the DLI (DownLine Load) option
configured into the Kernel, and the MOP_MOM layered subset installed
and running.  Then, it's fairly easy to set up the MOP_MOM listener
for the DECservers.  I've been running a DS100 for nearly a year, 
and I just fired up a DS200/MC earlier this week.

If Megan and Don will write me (bkort@musenet.org) and let me know
what resources you already have, I'll talk you through the rest of it.
Or, if your Ultrix host is online on the Internet, I could even log
in and do the setup for you.  Or Megan, if you are located in the
Boston area, you could bring your machine over, as I live in Bedford.

Barry Kort



