the alpha-dec-osf3.2.

When there is an EOM-encountered. I return
ENOSPC (errno 28)  within xxx_write().
I  also set bp->b_error to ENOSPC and set
bp->b_flags |= B_ERROR within xxx_strategy.

According to man pages, write() should return -1 and
set errno to ENOSPC.
Instead errno  was 0 while write() return 
something else ( i.e.. (count != write(fd, buf, count)) and
count not equal to -1)
